      "writtenOn": "2022-09-30T17:09:33Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I think there should be a comment here that this lerp is doing a linear interpolation on logarithmic values of brightness per channel but should be the same lerp done by the gradient shader which may be different. Now, we\u0027re at the moment usually drawing into an N32 surface for which this is true (the gradients are always too dark in the middle), but if we ever wanted to change that this would also need to be re-visited. However, with glyphs as drawables this may not always be the case anymore, and gradients may draw differently depending on the destination (I hadn\u0027t considered this before with glyphs as drawables, but I should go think about it now).",
      "revId": "143a56faad143a60f15970417a49248adb39d9de",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
