      "side": 1,
      "message": "Not a nit: Can\u0027t dereference `std::vector::end()`. I think we want `*(stops.end()-1)`?\n\n\nnit: I rather prefer this like\n\n```\nif (stops.size \u003c\u003d 1u) ||\n   (zeroRadiusStop \u003c *stops.begin() || *(stops.end()-1) \u003c zeroRadiusStop)\n{\n```\n\nTo make it obvious that even if there were no stops (I suppose we could `SkASSERT` at least one stop) this would just return, as well as make it obvious that this is a range check for `zeroRadiusStop` being outside the `stops` range. And when the `if` predicate is split across multiple lines I just find it easier to read if the `{` is on its own line so I can scan for where the predicate ends without getting confused.",
